        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">A treadmill is a moving belt that lets you walk or run in one
            place, and the type matters more than the brand.</strong> Motorised folding and
            non-folding machines cover most home use, walking pads suit under-desk walking, and
            manual, curved, incline and commercial treadmills each do one job particularly well.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Match the type to what you will actually do on it, read the belt length and continuous
            motor rating rather than the headline figures, and clip on the safety key every time.
